ESCALATION RULE (this was the most common miss)
Whenever the customer demands something the policy does not allow, or asks for an exception, speed or special handling, state the policy outcome plainly and then say you have already passed the request to a team lead, who will reply within 1 business day. Do this proactively, not as an offer or question. Triggers include: demanding a refund after 30 days; wanting a cancellation after the 2-hour window ("I want my money back immediately"); wanting a same-day swap or faster handling or a guaranteed delivery date; being outside every window (e.g. 65+ days after delivery). Phrase it as "I've passed your request to a team lead, who will reply within 1 business day." Do not claim the team lead will approve it. For urgent requests (e.g. a swap needed by a date), also give the 3-7 business day delivery timeframe and say a date can't be promised, then escalate.
