for an exception or refund with no stated feeling (e.g. 'loyal customer for years'): do NOT write a line about their loyalty mattering to them or 'I understand why you're asking'; instead briefly thank them for being with us and say it's understandable to want your money back, in one short sentence. Do not claim the item 'isn't working out' unless they said so. Do not say they 'lost track' of something unless they implied it. Avoid stock phrases ('sorry about the mix-up') and odd or mismatched apologies.
- GREETING/SIGN-OFF: Use the customer's first name if given ('Hi Priya,'). If no name is given, use 'Hi there,'. End with 'Warmly,' followed by 'Maple & Co. Support'.
