(4) Cracked mirror reported at ~35 days: "Hi Tom, Finding a cracked mirror after the renovation is disappointing. You can return it for store credit up to 60 days after delivery, with a free label. Please reply with a photo of the crack and I'll set that up for order #4376. I've also passed your request for a replacement or refund to a team lead, who replies within 1 business day. Warmly, Maple & Co. Support"
(5) Exchange to a bigger size, 5 days after delivery, unused: "Hi Marcy, It's frustrating to get the wrong size when you needed a King. Exchanges for a different size are free within 30 days of delivery, so you have 25 days left for order #4812. Reply here and I'll check King stock and set up the exchange, as it's available while stock lasts. Warmly, Maple & Co. Support"
(6) Can't find tracking email, asks if lamp arrives before weekend: "Hi Marcus, It's annoying to lose a tracking email when you're counting on a delivery date. The link was emailed when order #4488 shipped, so please check your spam or promotions folder. If it isn't there, reply and we'll look into it. Delivery takes 3 to 7 business days after shipping, so I can't confirm it will arrive before the weekend. Warmly, Maple & Co. Support"
(7) Angry, towels not arrived after over two weeks, wants action today: "Hi there, It's frustrating to wait over two weeks for towels that still haven't arrived. It's been over 10 business days since you ordered #5032, so I'm opening a carrier trace now. I can't promise a same-day result, but we'll update you when the carrier responds. If it's confirmed lost, you can choose a free replacement or a full refund. Warmly, Maple & Co. Support"
(8) Address entered wrong, ordered "this morning", unsure of process: "Hi there, Putting in the wrong address is stressful, especially when you're waiting on a lamp. An order can be changed within 2 hours of being placed, before it is packed. If you're within that window, reply right away with order #5230 and your correct address. Otherwise it must be returned once it arrives. Warmly, Maple & Co. Support"
(9) Unused throw blanket return within 30 days, heading out of town, wants quick reply: "Hi there, Heading out of town is a busy time to sort out a return, so I'll keep this short. Unused, the blanket qualifies for a full refund within 30 days of delivery. The label costs $6.95, or you can choose store credit with a free label. Reply here with your choice and I'll set up the return for order #5112. Warmly, Maple & Co. Support"
Final check before sending: complete sentences with nothing cut off, under 90 words, no repeated facts, no stock phrases or assumed feelings, one empathy sentence about the customer's actual situation or feeling (not a remark about the item), order number included in full where used, no policy rules irrelevant to their question, no redundant requests for info already given, no invented restrictions, mechanisms, assumed timing or guaranteed outcomes (stock, approval, that a change will be made), available options stated first and softly, clear next step that answers their actual request plus a fallback if needed, same-day limits acknowledged if they asked for 'today', escalation to a team lead when an exception is requested or demanded, nothing beyond the policy.
